% Generate `server/feedback.py`: in-app feedback / bug reports for the packaged desktop app.
% Module-level functions, no class. `from __future__ import annotations`. Import base64, json, os;
% `datetime`/`timezone`; typing `Any, Optional`; `requests`; `from lib import app_paths`; and
% `from server import analytics`.

% Design contract — a submission ALWAYS does three things, in resilience order (state this in the
% module docstring, with the flow `submit -> append jsonl -> capture event -> maybe email`):
%   1. DURABLE FIRST — append a JSON line to `<app_paths.home()>/feedback.jsonl` so feedback is
%      never lost, even with no network and no keys.
%   2. METADATA-ONLY ANALYTICS — pass the raw body to `analytics.capture`, which scrubs it
%      (`message` -> `message_len`) so the body never reaches analytics (see analytics.py).
%   3. BEST-EFFORT EMAIL — try the public relay first, direct Resend as fallback. Neither path may
%      raise into the caller; the full body goes ONLY to the local record and the email.

## Constants
- `VALID_KINDS = {"bug", "feature", "other"}`; `MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = 5000`.
- `_RESEND_ENDPOINT = "https://api.resend.com/emails"`.
- `_DEFAULT_RELAY_URL = "https://www.opennolan.com/api/feedback"` — the developer's public relay
  (website `/api/feedback`) that holds the Resend secret server-side, so the distributed app ships
  no key. Use the canonical `www` host (not the apex) to avoid a redirect on POST. Override via
  `FEEDBACK_RELAY_URL` (tests set "" to disable, or a test URL).

## API
`FeedbackError(ValueError)` — invalid submission; the endpoint maps it to HTTP 400.

`submit(kind, message, email=None, diagnostics=None, debug_session=None) -> dict` — validate, then
run the three steps above in order, then return `{"stored": True, "emailed": <bool>}`.
- Validate: `kind` in `VALID_KINDS`; `message` required (non-empty after strip) and
  `<= MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS`; else raise `FeedbackError`.
- Record = `{ts, kind, message, email or None, diagnostics or None, debug_session or None}`
  (`ts` = current UTC isoformat), appended durably BEFORE any network call.
- `analytics.capture("feedback_submitted", {kind, message, has_email, has_diagnostics,
  has_debug_session, has_attachment})` — raw `message` (scrubbed downstream); `has_*` are booleans.
- `emailed = _maybe_relay(...) or _maybe_email(...)`.
- When `debug_session` is given (editor "Send debug report" flow), attach that session's raw NDJSON
  log to the email as a FILE (never in the body): pass `attachments=[att] if att else None` to both
  delivery paths.

`_debug_attachment(session) -> Optional[dict]` — a Resend attachment `{filename:
"debug-session-<session>.ndjson", content: <base64 of raw NDJSON>}`. Lazy-import `server.debug_log`
and call `read_session_bytes(session)`. Returns `None` for a falsy session or ANY exception (missing/
bad/unreadable) — feedback must still send. Never raises.

`_maybe_email(kind, message, email, diagnostics, attachments=None) -> bool` — send via Resend iff
`RESEND_API_KEY` and `FEEDBACK_TO` are both set (else `False`). `from` = `FEEDBACK_FROM` env or
`"OpenNolan <onboarding@resend.dev>"`; subject `"OpenNolan <kind>: <first message line, 60-char
cap>"`; text body `"[<kind>] feedback from the OpenNolan app\n\n<message>"` with a `"Reply-to:
<email>"` block and a `--- diagnostics ---` block appended only when present. Include `reply_to` and
`attachments` keys only when set. POST with Bearer auth, `timeout=15`; return `status_code < 300`;
`requests.RequestException` -> `False`.

`_maybe_relay(kind, message, email, diagnostics, attachments=None) -> bool` — POST to the relay URL
(`FEEDBACK_RELAY_URL` env or `_DEFAULT_RELAY_URL`; falsy -> `False`) so it emails server-side with
its own key. JSON `{kind, message, email, diagnostics}` plus `attachments` when set; add header
`X-Feedback-Token` when `FEEDBACK_RELAY_TOKEN` is set. `timeout=15`. Non-2xx -> `False`; on 2xx
return the body's `emailed` flag, treating a non-JSON body as delivered (`True`);
`requests.RequestException` -> `False`.

## Helpers
- `_feedback_path()` = `app_paths.home() / "feedback.jsonl"`.
- `_append_record(record)` — `mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` the parent, open "a" (utf-8),
  write `json.dumps(record) + "\n"`. `O_APPEND` keeps one small line atomic vs a concurrent reader.
